      "math_academy_id": "e-3985",
      "problem": "Evaluate $\\log_{2} \\left(\\dfrac 1 {8} \\right).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite $\\dfrac{1}{8}$ as a power of $2$ (the base of the logarithm) as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{8} = \\dfrac{1}{2^3} = 2^{-3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\log_{2} \\left(\\dfrac 1 {8} \\right)= \\log_{2} (2^{-3}).\n$$\n\nNow we can proceed as usual. The log of a power of the base equals the power itself:\n\n$$\n\\log_b(b^x) = x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $b=2$ and $x=-3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\log_{2}( 2^{-3} )= -3.\n$$",
